qcom-va-driver (1.1.1+gitee8622c-0diting2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * patches/0001: the encoder stamps its input a frame apart instead of a
    microsecond. The firmware's rate control budgets by those stamps: with
    the microsecond stamps of upstream, CBR came out at 734 kbit/s whether
    1, 4 or 20 Mbit/s were asked for (docs/VIDEO_ENCODE.md).

 -- ubuntu-diting local build <ubuntu-diting@localhost>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:05:00 +0000

qcom-va-driver (1.1.1+gitee8622c-0diting1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Local build for the Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting) from upstream ee8622c: the
    VA-API driver with an encoder over the iris encoder (docs/VIDEO_ENCODE.md).
    GPU copy, CDSP and Vulkan video processing are off; the CPU copy is built
    in.
  * Installed as qcom_drv_video.so only. Not as msm_drv_video.so nor
    v4l2_drv_video.so: those two names stay with libva-v4l2-stateful, which
    keeps decoding for the browsers, so the two packages stand side by side
    and a program picks this one with LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=qcom.
  * Second package, qcom-va-driver-tests: upstream's hardware tests, built
    for the phone.

 -- ubuntu-diting local build <ubuntu-diting@localhost>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0000
